{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.SkeinBarAntisymmetry","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.SkeinBarAntisymmetry","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.skein_bar_antisymmetry_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.skein_bar_antisymmetry_full","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-bar-antisymmetry.lean#L69-L82","doc":"**Skein bar-antisymmetry** (Proposition):\n\nThe Skein relation in any commutative ring is antisymmetric\nunder simultaneous swap of (L_+, L_-) and (q, q⁻¹), and the\nbar-image relation is logically equivalent to the original. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.skein_bar_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.skein_bar_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-bar-antisymmetry.lean#L56-L67","doc":"**Both sides flip together**: applying bar to the Skein relation\nmultiplies both sides by −1, leaving the equation unchanged\n(consistency of bar-antisymmetry). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.bar_Lp_minus_Lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.bar_Lp_minus_Lm","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-bar-antisymmetry.lean#L52-L54","doc":"**Sign-flip identity**: the bar-image of (Lp − Lm) is −(Lp − Lm). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.bar_q_minus_qInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.bar_q_minus_qInv","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-bar-antisymmetry.lean#L48-L50","doc":"**Sign-flip identity**: the bar-image of (q − q⁻¹) is −(q − q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.skein_bar_antisymmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.skein_bar_antisymmetry","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-bar-antisymmetry.lean#L35-L46","doc":"**Bar-antisymmetry of the Skein relation.**\n\nSubstituting (Lp, Lm, q, qInv) ↦ (Lm, Lp, qInv, q) into the\nSkein relation yields the negation of the original relation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:skein-bar-antisymmetry","label":"prop:skein-bar-antisymmetry","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-bar-antisymmetry.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.SkeinRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SkeinBarAntisymmetry.SkeinRel","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-bar-antisymmetry.lean#L30-L33","doc":"The Skein relation: L_+ − L_− = (q − q⁻¹) · L_0, evaluated in\nthe field of fractions (or any ring where q is a unit). ","signatureChunk":0}]}